  "workflow-session-release" [label="Sessions released\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Coordinator integrates outcomes, records any pending decisions with a receiving owner, closes completed assignments and releases their sessions. Do not confuse an idle planner with an active owner.\nblocker: Coordinator integration and selected workflow delivery/acceptance remain unfinished; bounded worker assignments have ended.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md"];
  "workflow-communication-acceptance" [label="Communication\nacceptance\nBLOCKED", shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Native worker delivery worked; an actual active-window independent dashboard-session send/return exchange now verified. Historical failure cause remains unproven, reconnect lifetime and external/cloud delivery remain unverified. Acceptance scope still awaits selection.\nblocker: Required communication paths and their acceptance contract have not been selected; native packet delivery does not establish legacy MCP send recovery.\nplan_gap: Native subagent send/return worked. Original independent-thread endpoint failure cause lacks evidence; current read connectivity does not prove sends or receipt. Select whether retained-file/manual receipt suffices or a bounded live send/ack test is required.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md"];
  "host-codex-config-drift" [label="Host config drift\nOwnership unknown\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Read-only triage complete:35additions/3deletions are live via ~/.codex/config.toml Stow symlink. All delta literals observed in OTel session09:47:59UTC before its telemetry edits. Git baseline authors do not attribute dirty edits. Categories: internal model-tooltip state; browser backend/version/path; browser origin policies; plugin/hook enablement/trust; undocumented analytics flag. Preserved unchanged; OTel remains complete.\nblocker: All dirty-delta authorship remains unknown; successful writer evidence absent in bounded local search. Live configuration disposition still needs intent/implementation review; no revert or commit authorized.\nowner: 01a0f18c-14b4-78e2-a7ef-91e0d7b23f0a\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nnext_step: Coordinator retains ownership. Review intended live settings and separate runtime trust/tooltip state before proposing a focused dotfiles disposition; preserve originals until then.\nSources: docs/coordination/current.json, docs/development-environments.md"];
  "thesis-ready" [label="Thesis ready\nBLOCKED", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="One exact selected PDF has supported claims, traceable exposition/evidence, adequate required content, and Jörn’s readiness judgment at the recorded PASS threshold: only minor issues Kai could leave Jörn to fix in about two hours; borderline is FAIL. No present whole-PDF verdict establishes this.\nblocker: Thesis execution stopped; selected-source repairs, claim/evidence checks, frozen candidate and whole-PDF human judgment remain unfinished.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoff.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md", penwidth=2, fontsize=14];
  "code-evidence-ready" [label="Code and evidence\nBLOCKED", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Thesis algorithm/numerical promises match public API contracts and bounded correspondence evidence; every displayed example/count/figure/certificate resolves to its actual producer and public or working-repository availability. Tests are evidence layers, not unrestricted theorem proofs.\nblocker: Current claim-to-implementation and artifact-availability completeness has not been established; scoped checks remain unselected.\nplan_gap: No need for blanket code cleanup or a universal solver formalization; inspect exactly what retained claims require.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: crates/README.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md", penwidth=2, fontsize=14];
  "reproduction-ready" [label="Reproduction ready\nBLOCKED", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Document and check the agreed code → experiment output → figure-copy → PDF flows; name environments, tool versions, original LICCA route/timings/specs and byte-identical versus accepted comparisons. Retain explicitly accepted historical limitations; smoke success is not full evidence.\nblocker: Playbook completeness versus thesis promises is unverified; no scoped clean-environment verification package is selected.\nplan_gap: Missing completeness evidence is an open question, not a confirmed broken producer or automatic permission for costly reruns.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/reproducibility.md, docs/project-facts.md, submit/archive-closure-checklist.md", penwidth=2, fontsize=14];
  "thesis-scope-disposition" [label="Scope disposition\nBLOCKED", shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Clarify whether the closed named DS method table meets Jörn’s intended scope; explicitly select, omit or defer remaining optional results. Preserve required result areas and support-strength caveats; do not count ledger rows against the historical approximate repertoire size.\nblocker: Overall DS scope classification remains uncertain pending Jörn; stopped execution supplies no new selection.\nplan_gap: Fixed-pentagon/symmetric-partner selection is unresolved; optional research validity does not create a thesis obligation.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nnext_step: Present exact current-source scope choices separately from reader concerns and optional research.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "thesis-source-repairs" [label="Source repairs\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Verify suggested issues against the current selected source before patching; apply supported bridge/orientation/provenance repairs and disposition DS/AI annotations without transferring verdicts from older drafts. No broad rewrite or missing-proof claim follows from the backlog.\nblocker: No thesis execution window selected; source-aware repair packets and DS scope disposition remain unselected.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md"];
  "thesis-claims-supported" [label="Claims supported\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Check relevant paper → formal proof → implementation/experiment → thesis arrows. In particular preserve L10-N/L10-N+ equality-family and upper-section-curvature caveats, and the conditional/generic flow theorem versus bounded production correspondence.\nblocker: Current rendered claim audit and post-repair candidate-wide support check are unperformed; the 25 September scientific view is dated.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/consolidation/2026-09-24/claim-disposition.md"];
  "thesis-frozen-candidate" [label="Frozen candidate\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Build only thesis/main.tex after selected edits; inspect changed pages plus adjacent floats/references/appendix continuations; record source revision and PDF hash and intentionally reconcile retained build verification. The existing frozen PDF has seven known input mismatches.\nblocker: Stopped thesis run; source/support/reproduction work unfinished and no current accepted frozen candidate.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: thesis/README.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md"];
  "thesis-human-pass" [label="Human PASS\nBLOCKED", shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Jörn judges one inspected frozen candidate and takes responsibility for it; when satisfied, the recorded flow sends it to Kai, incorporates feedback and then hands in without another full Kai review. Final grading is one-time and distinct from diagnostic reviews.\nblocker: Frozen inspected candidate and Jörn’s readiness to review it are absent; no fast Kai-review arrangement is established.\nplan_gap: Local annotation repairs and agent reviews do not establish whole-chapter or whole-PDF human acceptance.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoff.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "reproduction-acceptance" [label="Reproduction checks\nBLOCKED", shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="After the claim/output map, define which clean-environment producer/comparison checks are necessary, estimate substantial costs, select them and retain evidence or an explicitly accepted limitation. Do not rerun --full workflows or replace retained outputs merely to tidy status.\nblocker: Concrete claimed-artifact comparison scope, environment, cost and execution selection are absent.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/reproducibility.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "project-delivery-disposition" [label="Delivery and\narchive\nBLOCKED", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Establish current administrative status and requirements first; do not infer an outstanding hand-in from old deadline/unsubmitted notes. Prepare the accepted continuation/archive payload with rights/data dispositions, exact reviewed commit, checked PDF, inventory/hashes and metadata. External submission/publication remains a separate Jörn-authorized action.\nblocker: Current submission status/rules and closure-time payload/rights/data review are unverified; no release candidate or external action is selected.\nplan_gap: Accepted Zenodo direction is not a created/published record or DOI. Current closure can record an already-completed administrative action once verified.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/project-facts.md, submit/archive-closure-checklist.md, docs/reproducibility.md", penwidth=2, fontsize=14];
  "project-close" [label="Project close\nBLOCKED", shape=box, fillcolor="#fce9e5", color="#ba6251", tooltip="Coordinator reconciles selected outcomes and caveats, current scientific synthesis when its sources/route change, retained completion evidence and continuation constraints; release all project-owned assignments/sessions. Optional research remains explicitly disposed rather than silently included.\nblocker: Required branch outcomes and human/delivery dispositions unfinished; selected worker integration and final release remain pending.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: Completion criterion mapped; no autonomous thesis run or external delivery is authorized.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "coordination-load-watch" [label="Load supervision\nRUNNING", shape=box, fillcolor="#e5effa", color="#3675ac", tooltip="Read-only OTel/local-metadata checker integrated; independent review resolved four misleading cases and all 13 focused tests pass. A fresh-context observer checks now and every four minutes for three further checks, reports changed warnings to root and then stops. No current alerts at 17:30:52Z; semantic backlog and billed spend remain unknown. Observer role lacks native collaboration send tools; its available TUI send transport delivered reports to root. Absolute-time scheduling avoids shortened waits when input interrupts sleep.\nowner: /root/coordination_load_observer\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Selected bounded implementation and supervision; four observations over about twelve minutes, no permanent service or thesis execution.\nnext_step: Receive the remaining timed observations, act on material alerts, then release observer ownership and retain the outcome.\nSources: scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, docs/coordination/README.md"];
  "__completed" [label="DONE · owners released\nShared coordination\nLocal guidance\nWorkstation OTel\nSkill proposal\nKnowledge proposal\nProposal integration\nSemantic project map\nSupport-route proposal\nAccounting proposal\nProject completion map", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#e7f1e8", color="#93918c", tooltip="Separate coordination, browser views and reusable knowledge\nCanonical coordination and browser source contract complete; five HTTP checks passed. Prior Chrome inspection unavailable.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nRoute process knowledge into project collaboration guidance\nLocal collaboration rules and knowledge routing complete; link/state checks passed. Behavioral and post-compaction performance untested.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: AGENTS.md, AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/knowledge/README.md\n\nSet up authorized workstation-only OpenObserve telemetry\nLive workstation logs/traces/metrics API-verified after daemon restart. Host implementation complete; maintenance belongs to ~/.dotfiles/INSTALL.md. Browser login unverified.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/otel-design.md\n\nPrepare repository-owned skill migration\nReviewable local skill/discovery migration proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Candidate, activation and fresh-client acceptance remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nPlan process-knowledge cleanup and behavioural evaluation\nReviewable two-link cleanup and bounded forward-pilot proposal returned; planner assignment ended. Cleanup and pilot remain unselected.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nReview and consolidate returned skill and knowledge proposals\nReviewed migration and knowledge proposals against returned environment/accounting findings. Recommend nine project-local skills with Claude adapters, conditional host capabilities and retained-packet handoffs; defer controlled behavioral pilot and new messaging infrastructure. Concrete package selection remains Jörn’s decision; no skill activation or execution approval is inferred.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md, docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nSemantic msc-math project map dashboard\nSemantic DOM portfolio view completed in dedicated design session: whole msc-math goal, completion branches, interactive outcome/status/owner/blocker/scope/evidence/next-step nodes and shared prerequisite links. Live desktop/390px and320px fixture checked; no horizontal overflow.15second refresh preserves open state/focus. Root integrated source/dependency checks and8 HTTP tests.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md\n\nDefine support and handoff routes across selected environments\nRead-only supported-route matrix returned: local .agents source plus proposed Claude links/import; retained packets and manual host handoff initially. Independent-thread live delivery and SSH persistence remain unverified; Codex Cloud privileged-image/R2 bootstrap assumptions are not validated for Claude.\nplan_gap: Claude fresh-clone setup/discovery, cloud-to-host handoff, remote-device review access and reconnect/session continuity have no agreed acceptance route. Required support versus explicitly deferred capabilities is unresolved.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md, docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nDefine truthful usage and spending observations\nRead-only recommendation returned: current.json and retained outcomes own durable PM state; OpenObserve is diagnostic. Optional explicit packet-event JSONL-to-OTel helper only if selected; no broker/database. Token/time observations are not billing; quota/USD unknown and independent-root/cloud usage is not covered.\nplan_gap: Comparable cloud/Pro usage, semantic task/message journaling and budget-enforcement mechanics are undefined. Numeric thresholds are not agreed; the selected delivery may explicitly defer automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: AGENTS.md.commentary.md, docs/development-environments.md\n\nWhole-project completion map and dependency projection\nWhole msc-math outcome/dependency map retained: workflow subproject, thesis support/prose and human PASS, code/evidence, reproduction, actual delivery/archive and closure. Twelve independent read-only candidates plus optional research/writing routes are visible without execution authorization. Semantic dashboard is primary; DOT/SVG source-hash projection checks pass.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md"];
  "__parked" [label="UNSELECTED / PARKED · no execution\nCommunication diagnosis · BLOCKED\nSkill migration candidate · PARKED\nKnowledge cleanup / pilot · PARKED\nCloud automation · PARKED\nThesis execution STOPPED · PARKED\nOptional result routes · PARKED\nOpen research packages · PARKED\nWriting method trial · PARKED", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#f1f0ed", color="#93918c", tooltip="Determine why agent communication tools failed\nBounded local diagnosis finished. Same daemon persisted through failures; multiple TUI MCP server processes turned over. Stale endpoint binding is plausible, but old-port ownership, shutdown/rebind evidence and original cause are unavailable. Current list verifies reads only.\nblocker: Historical endpoint ownership/binding evidence is unavailable; current successful reads do not establish original cause or legacy send recovery.\nplan_gap: Capture failing URL, socket owner/PID and endpoint-binding lifecycle events on the next natural failure. Do not launch repeated investigation or restart the shared daemon.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/current.json\n\nOptional local skill candidate, activation and fresh-client tests\nProposed nine-skill local package, Claude discovery adapters and focused acceptance route. Keep outside loaded paths until selected. This is a candidate route, not an assignment.\nplan_gap: Initial instruction was inspect/plan/discuss first; migration and activation selection absent.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/skill-migration-plan.md\n\nOptional knowledge cleanup and forward pilot\nChoose retain-and-observe, two-link cleanup only, or cleanup plus bounded A/E pilot. No model calls or cleanup are launched by this plan.\nplan_gap: Scope, owner and resources have not been selected; broader cases and post-compaction validation remain unperformed.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/coordination/knowledge-evaluation-plan.md\n\nPossible cloud communication, setup and accounting automation\nExternal surfaces remain outside workstation telemetry. Live cloud messaging, detailed returned event logs and enforcement are possible mechanisms; required support and value are undecided.\nplan_gap: No agreed need, design, acceptance contract or authorization for cloud automation.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Only the recorded selected assignment is authorized; future activation/execution remains separately selected.\nSources: docs/development-environments.md\n\nThesis execution — STOPPED\nPrevious thesis completion run remains stopped. Backlog availability does not authorize a new execution window.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: STOPPED; no autonomous thesis execution window.\nSources: docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nReview optional research/result selection\nReviewed but unselected results include the fixed-pentagon/symmetric-partner bound, harmonic blind directions, ridge circulation, moment counterexample and joint-representation separations. Research validity/interest is not thesis selection or novelty acceptance.\nplan_gap: No exact optional result is selected for integration; the general zonotope bound remains conjectural/paused.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded statement/evidence/value comparison before any research execution or thesis addition.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nStructure a bounded future mathematical research packet\nThe dated scientific view records F=11/global HKO questions as outside the submission route; project facts distinguish non-generic arbitrary-polytope support from generic smooth-branch results. These are possible future questions, not current theorem obligations or assigned experiments.\nplan_gap: Exact question, owner evidence baseline, useful alternatives and resources have not been selected; recheck source owners before promoting historical open questions.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded problem-structuring packet; no large proof search, producer or Pro handoff follows automatically.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/dashboard/thesis.html\n\nConsider a discriminating authoring-workflow trial\nA current-source passage trial may inform authoring value, but local trials cannot certify whole-thesis readiness. Source repairs have independent value and do not depend on this optional mechanism.\nplan_gap: No trial candidate, success criterion, cost or human-review package selected; retrospective writing outcomes are not a general reliable method.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a concrete trial only if it could change the authoring route enough to justify its cost.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_thesis" [label="THESIS · READY IF SELECTED\nFoundations / QP\nVariation / certificate\nProduct proof bridges\nDS reader disposition\nFigures / numerical example\nAI reflection map", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check current foundations and QP exposition\nRead Chapters 2 and 4 against backlog items 1: terminology, Rudolf input/output, cyclic-word operation and dependence/vertex-replacement bridges. Return surviving/solved/withdrawn findings with exact source locations; no edits or theorem strengthening.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only Chapter 2/4 packet in its own worktree.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck variation and HKO certificate navigation\nRead Chapters 6/7 and HKO appendix against backlog item 2; separate finite predicates and geometric implication. The certificate and slope-to-neighborhood proof are reported present. No certificate recomputation.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-navigation review; coordinate Chapter 7 edits with the claim packet.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck product-family finite and limiting proof bridges\nRead Chapters 9–11 against backlog item 3: ordered pairings, finite vertex/alternation calculations, equality classification, product-position squeeze and Hausdorff/capacity-continuity bridge. Preserve exact/numerical distinctions.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select an independent product-proof source packet; report exact surviving bridges before edits.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nDispose of reader concerns against the selected DS chapter\nMap retained human comments to current Chapter 8/appendix: applied, absent, context-accepted or older-draft-only. Preserve accepted correlation/area text, retrospective bounds and explicitly unresolved random_F8_s3_45. Human acceptance and overall DS scope remain separate.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a source-aware DS disposition packet; do not import old rejection as a current verdict.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nCheck visualization purposes and certified numerical example\nInspect Chapters 12–14 for panel purpose/inference limits and the requested concrete certified numerical example; return a scoped proposal using existing code/evidence without launching producers.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only example/provenance design packet before implementing or running it.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md\n\nVerify AI annotation repairs against the selected source\nCheck selected Chapter 15 against the mapped v3 repairs; no confirmed annotation defect remains. Preserve factual disclosure separately from reflection and record source drift or unknown whole-chapter acceptance.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded source-map check; do not rewrite unflagged AI prose.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md"];
  "__candidates_evidence" [label="EVIDENCE · READY IF SELECTED\nChapter 7 claim check\nCode correspondence\nArtifact traceability", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Check rendered Chapter 7 claims and PDF/source identity\nIdentify source revision/PDF identity, then compare L10-N/L10-N+ rendered statement, equality family and upper-section-curvature caveat against 24 September disposition and non-HKO rational/analytic packet. If no matching PDF is available, report that prerequisite; do not treat the older frozen PDF as current.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select the bounded rendered-PDF claim audit; no expensive verifier rerun.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/consolidation/2026-09-24/claim-disposition.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/README.md, experiments/hko-local-maximum/non-hko/PROOF.md\n\nCheck retained algorithm and numerical contract boundaries\nTrace retained capacity/numerics/flow promises to crate APIs and focused evidence owners; distinguish theorem assumptions, bounded tests and optimized production correspondence. Return exact claim/contract gaps and recommended focused checks; no blanket implementation rewrite.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select read-only claim/API/evidence mapping in a separate worktree; test execution requires its chosen packet.\nSources: crates/README.md, docs/project-facts.md, ARCHITECTURE.md\n\nResolve displayed examples, counts and public artifact references\nMap named KKT/comparison/product counts, figures and annotated HKO listing to canonical packets and actual tracked/registered/public availability. Existing local files do not establish a public commit or remote download promise.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: evidence\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded current-claim-to-artifact inventory; preserve producer-owned outputs.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_reproduction" [label="REPRODUCTION · READY IF SELECTED\nReproduction inventory", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Compare the reproduction playbook with retained thesis promises\nInspect source-to-output-to-figure-to-PDF instructions, versions, LICCA timing/specs and comparison policies against the two-year target. Return complete/unknown/missing routes and cost estimates; no full producers or deletion experiment.\nplan_gap: Technically independent bounded candidate, currently unassigned and unselected; stopped thesis scope still applies.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a read-only playbook/output inventory; stage specific verification proposals afterward.\nSources: docs/reproducibility.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
  "__candidates_release" [label="RELEASE · READY IF SELECTED\nOfficial status check\nArchive preparation", fontsize=11, fillcolor="#fff7dc", color="#93918c", tooltip="Establish current submission status and official requirements\nPrepare a bounded check of current submission status, official rules and AI-disclosure requirements. Ask Jörn/current official sources when selected; never infer remaining hand-in or missed deadlines from historical notes.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select current status/rules inquiry; no external submission or message is authorized.\nSources: docs/project-facts.md, docs/coordination/handoff.md\n\nInventory closure-time rights, data and archive gaps\nCompare current payload/registry to accepted continuation/Zenodo checklist: rights notices, private/disposable material, useful artifacts, clean-cache materialization, exact reviewed commit/PDF, metadata and exterior publication. Return dispositions/questions without deleting, packing or publishing.\nplan_gap: Unassigned and unselected; current administration/closure facts need inspection.\nproject: release\nauthorization: Unselected candidate; Jörn must select a bounded packet before execution.\nnext_step: Select a bounded read-only closure inventory in its own worktree.\nSources: submit/archive-closure-checklist.md, docs/project-facts.md"];
